This archive is a Python implementation of the nested CSEOF operator
recorded in:

  Kim, S. Y., Cautionary Remarks on Nested Cyclostationary Empirical
  Orthogonal Function Analysis, J. Atmos. Oceanic Technol., submitted.

It is not the FORTRAN of K.-Y. Kim, not the MATLAB of B. D. Hamlington,
and not an official port of either. Those originals are not included
and are not redistributed.

The nested sequence (ordinary EOF, modified-sinc demodulation at k/T,
packed coefficients, second EOF, harmonic synthesis onto a nested
calendar) is described in the published CSEOF literature, including
Kim and Wu (1999) and applications that execute the distributed nested
code. Mathematical methods are not copyrighted. This repository claims
copyright only in the new Python expression (MIT License).

Discrete samples of the weighting window follow the 2010 MATLAB
weight.m as recorded in the paper, including the lag grid of that
file. The FORTRAN WEIGHT routine of cseofx.f uses a different lag
grid. Filter centers remain k/T. Packed-coefficient energy and
reconstruction rmse in the paper are for the MATLAB window. This
archive is written to match that MATLAB operator, not to replace it
with the FORTRAN window.

Do not cite this software as Kim and North (1996, 1997) cyclostationary
covariance eigenanalysis. That writing is a different matrix.
